course: dictionary
lesson: 55
title: Accuse and the accused
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To accuse someone is to say that they did something wrong or bad. You accuse a person of doing something, and the pattern is always «accuse someone of something». «In Egypt Joseph refused to do wrong, but she falsely accused him and he was put in prison.» The clues are «falsely», which means not true, and «put in prison», which tells you the accusation was serious.
explain: Accuse is a verb, so it changes: accuses, accused, accusing. In a court, the accused is the person on trial, and the word is also used as a noun. Think of a school playground: if someone says you broke the window, they are accusing you, even before anyone checks.
explain: Accusing someone is not the same as proving they did it. «Accusing without proof» is one of the worst things you can do, because an innocent person suffers. The words around accuse, like proof, court and innocent, are your clues that this is a serious word about fairness.
fact: To accuse someone means to say they did something wrong or bad.
fact: The pattern is «accuse someone of something», for example «accused him of lying».
fact: In a court, «the accused» is the person who is on trial.
fact: A person accused of a crime is innocent until a court decides.
fact: «Accuse» is a verb, with forms accuses, accused and accusing.
exercise: «She falsely accused him and he was put in prison.» What does accused mean here? | Gave him a present | *Said that he had done something wrong | Thanked him for helping | Asked him to come to dinner
exercise: In a court, who is the accused? | *The person on trial | The judge who listens to the case | The people who watch from the seats | The lawyer who asks questions
exercise: Complete the pattern: you accuse someone ___ something. | into | by | *of | for
test: Jayden says, «To accuse someone is just to tell a fact.» What does accuse actually mean? | To tell someone the time | To say that someone is very kind | *To say that someone did something wrong or bad | To run away quickly
test: Why is a person accused of a crime still innocent at first? | Because they have already said sorry | *Because a court has not yet decided that they did it | Because they are the judge | Because they always win their cases
exam: Which advice comes from this lesson? | Accuse everyone just to be safe | *You should not accuse someone without proof | Only accuse people you do not like | Proof does not matter when you accuse someone
